  "transcript": {
    "answer": "Agent pods run on the external floor (re-cinq/floor), not in Lore. The floor's own cluster agent runs each agent in a Kubernetes pod, as an Agent custom resource (CR) per assembly-line node (ADR-031). Lore's stations service only does the deterministic steps. Lore holds no Kubernetes client of its own, so it doesn't start the pods itself. The coordinator, Lore's own 'lore-agent' service, runs on GKE in the lore-agent namespace. The legacy LoreTask path (CRD, loretask-controller and claude-runner Job pods) is removed, as are Lore's own cluster agent and floor, which were deleted on 2026-10-02.",
